00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:05.030 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  hi  dino here in this video we will get to  know  apogee's api analytics  there are three big pieces to managing  an api program exposing your apis  enabling others to consume your apis and  then  measuring that activity apis are  foundational for digital business  so it's very important to have complete  visibility  into api performance you want to track  developer usage api usage trends  error rates geographic distribution  all of these metrics and more are  available to you through the apigee edge  platform  so you can analyze your digital business  in real time  let me show you some of what you get  navigate to the analytics menu  on the left hand side let's take a look  the api proxy performance chart  will show traffic volumes and response  times for your apis  this is such valuable insight some  customers create an  apigee pass-through proxy on existing  services just to get this view  you can view data for a specific proxy  or all proxies  look back an hour a day a week  or more and it's built in you don't have  to do anything to get this  so nice this report can be a great  resource for your developers  and devops team  the cache performance chart shows  utilization of the built-in apigee edge  cache for your apis  this is really handy for helping to  optimize performance and efficiency  the geo map shows you the geographic  source of traffic  it's marvelous to be able to track api  proxy usage  by geo to see where usage originates  the latency analysis chart is invaluable  when managing to a response time goal  stable performance is key for a quality  user experience  this apogee chart shows tp50  tp95 and tp99  that's average response time as well as  95th  and 99th percentile when you have spikes  in tp99 it indicates that other pieces  in your system are not delivering stable  performance under load  this chart pinpoints that problem  the traffic composition report shows you  the top proxies  products apps or developers by traffic  volumes  obviously valuable when managing an api  program  and you can create your own custom  reports based on the individual metrics  that are collected by apogee edge  like latency ip address path  and response status code  this is just a quick sample to get these  charts for your traffic  all you need to do is create an api  proxy in apigee edge  and direct client applications to use it  and of course all of the data presented  visually in these charts is available  via an api so you can export it into  your own  analysis tools okay  that's the quick introduction to apogee  edge analytics  it gives you visibility into key  performance and operating metrics for  your apis  and if you want to know more dive into  the product documentation  or visit the community till next time  keep it digital

